(SECTION 1: ESSENTIAL AVIATION TERMINOLOGY) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(* AFT: The rear or tail section of the aircraft cabin.) Tj
T*
(* FORWARD \(FWD\): The front portion of the aircraft, near the flight deck.) Tj
T*
(* GALLEY: The kitchen area of an aircraft where meals and beverages are prepared.) Tj
T*
(* BULKHEAD: A dividing wall separating different sections or cabins \(e.g., Business & Economy\).) Tj
T*
(* CROSSCHECK: Verification by cabin crew that doors are armed or disarmed properly.) Tj
T*
(* DEPLANING: The process of passengers exiting the aircraft after landing.) Tj
T*
(* STERILE COCKPIT: Regulatory period below 10,000 feet where no non-essential communication) Tj
T*
(  between cabin crew and flight deck is permitted.) Tj
T*
(* TURBULENCE: Irregular atmospheric air motion categorized as Light, Moderate, or Severe.) Tj
T*
(* ZULU TIME \(UTC\): Universal Coordinated Time standard used across global aviation.) Tj
T*
(* AVSEC: Aviation Security protocols governed by the Bureau of Civil Aviation Security \(BCAS\).) Tj
T*
(* DGR: Dangerous Goods Regulations defining hazardous cargo and carriage rules.) Tj
T*
(* PAX: Universal airline abbreviation for passengers.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
