(SECTION 2: THE ICAO PHONETIC ALPHABET & COMMUNICATION) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Aviation relies on the International Civil Aviation Organization \(ICAO\) phonetic) Tj
T*
(alphabet to eliminate misunderstandings over radios and interphones.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(  A - ALPHA        H - HOTEL        O - OSCAR        V - VICTOR) Tj
T*
(  B - BRAVO        I - INDIA        P - PAPA         W - WHISKEY) Tj
T*
(  C - CHARLIE      J - JULIETT      Q - QUEBEC       X - X-RAY) Tj
T*
(  D - DELTA        K - KILO         R - ROMEO        Y - YANKEE) Tj
T*
(  E - ECHO         L - LIMA         S - SIERRA       Z - ZULU) Tj
T*
(  F - FOXTROT      M - MIKE         T - TANGO) Tj
T*
(  G - GOLF         N - NOVEMBER     U - UNIFORM) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(CABIN CREW PUBLIC ANNOUNCEMENT \(PA\) PRACTICE PROTOCOL:) Tj
T*
(  - Speak at an even tempo of 120-140 words per minute.) Tj
T*
(  - Pitch voice slightly lower than conversational tone to avoid microphone distortion.) Tj
T*
(  - Maintain warm, authoritative clarity during safety and welcome briefings.) Tj
T*
ET
